pokeheartgold-speed.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies the patches in name order): the port's per-part speed options
(docs/speed-options.md "Platinum and HeartGold/SoulSilver"), hooked where HeartGold's and SoulSilver's C decides each part's
pace; each hook asks port/game/speed_gen4.c, which reads the same settings Black's and Black 2's stand-ins read. At every
default setting each hook is exactly the game's own code path, so the route chain's frames are unchanged.
Text speed: text.c RunTextPrinter (the task every timed text printer runs once a frame: the field's and the battle's messages,
menus, every Options-speed caller and the fixed-speed ones) renders through PortTextSpeed_Render, which at Faster / Fastest /
Instant (4 / 8 / 1024 characters, PortSpeed4_TextChars) draws that many plain characters in the frame, clearing the character
wait before each; a control code, callback, key wait, scroll, pause or the end stops the frame as the game's one render did.
Instant printers (TEXT_SPEED_INSTANT) never reach the task and are unchanged. Platinum's twin is pokeplatinum-speed.patch.
Handover-ID: none (port-only)

